help_body='''<section class="section help-hero"><div class="container"><a class="text-link" href="/#downloads">← Back to downloads</a><p class="eyebrow">WINDOWS INSTALLATION HELP</p><h1>Why Windows says<br>“Windows protected your PC”.</h1><p class="section-intro">An unfamiliar app can trigger a SmartScreen warning. Here is what the message means, and how to make an informed choice.</p></div></section><section class="section help-content"><div class="container help-grid"><div class="prose"><h2>Reputation and publisher identity</h2><p>Microsoft Defender SmartScreen checks downloaded files using publisher and file reputation. SADPTools’ current Windows builds are unsigned, so Windows cannot show a verified publisher. A new version can also have little download history.</p><p>The warning alone does not establish whether a file is safe or malicious. Changing the download website does not remove the need for publisher trust.</p><h2>Check before continuing</h2><ol><li>Download from <a href="/#downloads">the SADPTools download section</a> using the links on this site.</li><li>Compare your file’s SHA-256 with the <a href="/download/checksums.txt">published checksums</a>. In PowerShell, run <code>Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 .\\your-downloaded-file.exe</code>. For the standalone package, check the ZIP before extracting it. A matching hash confirms file integrity; it does not establish a trusted publisher.</li><li>If you trust the download and want to proceed, select <strong>More info</strong>, then <strong>Run anyway</strong>, when Windows offers those options.</li></ol><p>If your organisation blocks the app or the option is absent, contact your IT administrator. Keep Windows security protections enabled; do not change managed policies to force the app to run.</p><h2>Installer or standalone?</h2><p>The installer includes the display runtime and handles setup. The standalone ZIP needs an existing WebView2 runtime; extract it before opening <code>SADPTools-windows-amd64.exe</code>. Both packages contain the same desktop application.</p><p><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/apps/package-and-deploy/smartscreen-reputation" rel="noopener">Microsoft’s explanation of SmartScreen reputation</a>.</p><a class="button" href="/#downloads">Choose a Windows download</a></div><figure class="warning-figure"><img src="/assets/windows-smartscreen.png" width="519" height="493" alt="Windows SmartScreen showing SADPTools-windows-amd64.exe with Unknown publisher and the Run anyway and Don't run buttons"><figcaption>The warning supplied by a SADPTools user. Wording and available options can vary with Windows version and policy.</figcaption></figure></div></section>'''
page('windows-help.html','Windows SmartScreen installation help — SADPTools','Understand the Windows unknown-publisher warning, verify your SADPTools download and choose the installer or standalone application.',help_body,{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'TechArticle','headline':'Windows SmartScreen installation help','description':'Why an unsigned SADPTools download can trigger a Windows warning and how to verify its integrity.','author':{'@type':'Person','name':'Paul Willard'},'url':base+'/windows-help.html','image':base+'/assets/windows-smartscreen.png'})
page('mac-help.html','Apple Mac installation & updates — SADPTools','Install SADPTools on Apple Silicon or Intel: universal DMG and ZIP, macOS permissions, Gatekeeper, Live View and manual updates.',mac_help_body,{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'TechArticle','headline':'Apple Mac installation and updates','description':'Install the universal SADPTools app, allow camera network access and update it manually.','author':{'@type':'Person','name':'Paul Willard'},'url':base+'/mac-help.html'})
privacy='''<section class="section"><div class="container narrow prose"><p class="eyebrow">PRIVACY</p><h1>Your work stays yours.</h1><h2>This website</h2><p>This site has no advertising, analytics trackers or account registration. Fonts, images, scripts and downloads are served from this domain. Your light or dark theme preference is saved in your browser’s local storage.</p><p>The web server receives normal request information, including IP address, requested path and user agent, and may retain access and error logs for operation and troubleshooting. Do not put credentials or customer information into a website URL.</p><h2>The desktop application</h2><p>On Windows, Linux and Apple Mac, SADPTools keeps site inventories and protected credentials on your computer. Saved credentials use Windows account protection or a master-passphrase vault on Linux and Mac. It does not require a cloud account or add telemetry. It connects to selected devices and services for operations you request or enable, including optional update checks. Exported files go where you choose.</p><p>The Windows display runtime is supplied by Microsoft and has its own update and privacy terms, included with the installer. Network cameras and services have their own behaviour and policies.</p><h2>Downloads</h2><p>The server retrieves and verifies published release files, then delivers them from sadptools.com. Downloading does not create an account or enrol you in a mailing list.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Contact <a href="mailto:paul@paulwillard.nz">Paul Willard</a> for questions about this website.</p></div></section>'''
